:INFO
Art. 67 Administration of justice
The appeal procedure is governed by the general provisions on the administration of federal justice.
|

:NOTE
Art. 67 — Amended by Annex No 92 of the Administrative Court Act of 17 June 2005, in force since 1 Jan. 2007 (AS 2006 2197; BBl 2001 4202).
|

:INFO
Art. 67a Public authority appeal
1 The Federal Office is entitled to make use of the rights of legal recourse available under federal and cantonal law in respect of decisions of the cantonal authorities in application of this Act and its implementing provisions.
2 …
|

:NOTE
Art. 67a — Inserted by No I 15 of the FA of 18 June 1999 on the Coordination and Simplification of Decision-making Procedures, in force since 1 Jan. 2000 (AS 1999 3071 3124; BBl 1998 2591).
Para. 2 — Repealed by Annex No 92 of the Administrative Court Act of 17 June 2005, with effect from 1 Jan. 2007 (AS 2006 2197; BBl 2001 4202).
